   "design": "Instructions are written in a structured authoring tool that enforces the plant's writer's guide and offers a library of standard steps, such as isolations and verifications. Equipment tags, setpoints and references come from the plant equipment database instead of being copied from drawings. A check confirms that every tag and setpoint matches the database and every reference is the current revision. No model writes or edits instruction text, because a changed procedure is a safety change. Walkdowns, comment resolution, revision and independent approval stay with people.",
